  "boundary": "This plan establishes fail-closed manual collection controls for the two Section 48 trust-specific evidence types that are not supplied by machine, rendered, device, assistive-technology, human, performance, energy, or provenance controls. A session-pass value is candidate evidence only. Real provider/privacy/security integration must be exercised, the record must exclude credentials and unnecessary private data, and separate governed review must accept the exact-source record before it can satisfy a Section 48 evidence group. No existing companion protocol automatically supplies or inherits these trust evidence types, and no record automatically establishes Section 48 acceptance, V1.7.1 lifecycle promotion, consumer eligibility, deployment, publication, or production acceptance."
